  "body": "D3b of the tool library plan (#3663): the rest of #3662.\n\n## Covered and remaining (#3662)\n\n| #3662 item | State | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| A tapered mill with a tip diameter or a ball tip | Covered on main by D1, PR #3929 (`tip_form`, `tip_diameter`, `.camtools` version 6) | `tool_library.rs::a_tip_form_round_trips_and_steps_the_version`; this PR adds the #3662 synthetic numbers: `converted_3662::the_3662_tapered_mills_round_trip_with_their_tips` |\n| A drawn cutter outline in a `.camtools` definition | Covered on main by D3a, PR #3906 (`cutter`, version 5) | `tool_library.rs::a_drawn_cutter_round_trips_through_the_library_file` |\n| A form mill with a drawn profile | Covered on main by D2, PR #3946 (`form_mill` with `form`) for outlines whose radius does not narrow upward | `tool_library.rs::a_form_mill_round_trips_with_its_outline` |\n| The #3662 synthetic form mill (one V tooth on a necked shank) | Covered by this PR: it is a single-form thread mill with its drawn cutter | `converted_3662::the_3662_form_mill_rides_the_file_as_a_necked_single_form_thread_mill` |\n| A single-form thread mill without a pitch range | This PR | see below |\n| The dovetail neck check without a tolerance | This PR | see below |\n| A general form mill whose outline narrows upward (an undercut form) | Remaining. `form_mill.rs` refuses it by name; the work stays with #896 | `form_mill.rs` module comment |\n| Operations that cut with a flat-tip or ball-tip taper | Remaining, outside #3662 (which asks for the file only). The operation doors refuse such a tool by name (`taper::is_unread_tip`) | `taper.rs` module comment |\n\n## What changed\n\n- `camcraft_tools::thread_mill::read_unstated_range`: a single-form thread mill whose definition has no `pitch_min` key reads as a range of its one stated pitch (`pitch_min = pitch`). The thread operation then cuts that pitch and refuses every other pitch by name (the existing `resolve_pitch` door). This is the narrowest range. It never widens what an operation accepts.\n- `ToolDto::pitch_min` is now `Option<f64>`. Only an absent key gets the one-pitch reading. A stated `pitch_min: 0` stays 0 and the sanity law refuses it by name, as before. So `edit_tool` cannot turn a stated 0 into another number. The writer is unchanged: it writes the key only when it is not 0.\n- The shipped catalog reader (`catalog_asset.rs`) reads an absent key in the same way.\n- `undercut.rs`: the dovetail neck check is `top < sr - NECK_MEETS`, with `NECK_MEETS = 1e-9` mm (float dust, the same slack as the lollipop check). The #3662 inch dovetail (0.24 in head, 0.0575 in high, 45 degrees, 1/8 in neck) puts its flank top one ulp under the neck in mm. It is now accepted. A neck 1e-6 mm or 0.002 mm wider is still refused.\n- `camcraft-mcp` skill: the thread-mill row says what an absent `pitch_min` means.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/3662-camtools-rest.md`.\n\n## Version step\n\nNone. This build writes no new key and no new value: a single-form mill that it writes always states `pitch_min`. Thus each file that this build writes is read by older builds. An older build refuses only a file without the key (for example from a converter), by the tool's name, as it did before. No file that older builds read changes meaning, so the change is not breaking.\n\n## Readings\n\n- #3662 dovetail in mm: `0.24*25.4 = 6.095999999999999`, flank top `1.5874999999999995`, neck radius `1.5875`.\n- #3662 form mill: diameter 8, flute length 1.6 (the tooth), pitch 1.6, form angle `2*atan(0.8/2) = 43.6` degrees, neck 2 mm radius from 1.6 to 9, shank 8 to 40. The thread operation refuses its 43.6 degree form by name.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft_tools::undercut::tests::a_neck_that_meets_the_flank_exactly_is_accepted`\n- `camcraft_tools::thread_mill::tests::an_unstated_range_reads_as_the_one_stated_pitch`\n- `camcraft_tools::catalog_asset::tests::a_catalog_single_form_thread_mill_without_a_range_cuts_its_one_pitch`\n- `app tool_library::converted_3662::a_single_form_thread_mill_without_a_pitch_range_loads`\n- `app tool_library::converted_3662::the_3662_form_mill_rides_the_file_as_a_necked_single_form_thread_mill`\n- `app tool_library::converted_3662::the_3662_tapered_mills_round_trip_with_their_tips`\n\nThe new app tests are a module of the existing `tool_library` binary (`crates/app/tests/tool_library/converted_3662.rs`), as `tool_library_holders/used_by.rs` is. No new test binary.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No UI change. The tool editor still seeds a range when the kind is picked; it shows a no-range tool as finest = coarsest.\n- No heavy step (P6, not P1).\n- A thread toolpath with a one-pitch single-form mill is not generated here; the operation reads the same `resolve_pitch`, pinned in `thread_mill.rs`.\n\n## Gate (Windows, winbuild)\n\nLog `C:\\camcraft-logs\\gate-3662-d94b3f7e8.log`, `HEAD: d94b3f7e852ea68c5766e26d88f67f3ab343a012`, base `origin/main` d94b9816d (merge-base = origin/main, so no trial merge was needed). `CAMCRAFT_NO_SEED=1`, `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=5`.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 16 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 4.1 min, `GATE EXIT: 0`. Steps: tools build, tools lib (148 passed, the three new unit tests named above among them), tools tap_hand, sim undercut_fixture_envelope, motion golden_undercut, app build, app lib (307 passed), app contour_dxf_sketch, mcp_undercut_fixture, plasma_cut_data, pocket_no_adaptive, sinker_electrode_body, sketch_project, tool_library (25 passed, the three `converted_3662` tests among them), tool_reservations_version, units_migrate.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` on the same head: `CLIPPY EXIT: 0` (`C:\\camcraft-logs\\clippy-3662-d94b3f7e8.log`).\n- Not run: `cargo xtask gate light`, the example catalog suites (no post or toolpath code changed), a heavy step (P6). The new tests were not run red before the fix on this lane.\n\nChangelog: A tool library or project file can hold a single-form thread mill without a pitch range: it cuts only its stated pitch. A dovetail cutter whose neck meets the flank exactly is accepted.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nEffort: high\n\n## Catalog timeout\n\nThe 60 s limit of `catalog_3d_rough_finish` failed once under load. This PR does not touch that path, and the failure reproduces on bare main under load. See issue #3975.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #3662\n\n",
